      "sentences": [
        {
          "text": "The lecturer appears to be elaborating on a nuanced distinction between closely related concepts.",
          "grammar": "appear to be＋現在分詞 / elaborate on / between",
          "ja": "講師は互いに密接に関連する概念の微妙な違いについて詳しく説明しているようです。",
          "type": "gist",
          "points": 40
        },
        {
          "text": "To elaborate on a nuanced distinction means to explain a subtle difference in considerably greater detail.",
          "grammar": "to不定詞主語 / mean to",
          "ja": "「elaborate on a nuanced distinction」とは、微妙な違いをかなり詳しく説明することを意味します。",
          "type": "gist",
          "points": 40
        },
        {
          "text": "The scatter plot illustrates a statistical association, whereas the diagram on the right depicts alternative forms of connection.",
          "grammar": "whereas",
          "ja": "散布図は統計的な関連を示している一方、右側の図は異なる形のつながりを示しています。",
          "type": "detail",
          "points": 40
        },
        {
          "text": "By presenting the two visual models side by side, the lecturer can highlight distinctions that might otherwise be overlooked.",
          "grammar": "By＋動名詞 / 関係代名詞that / might",
          "ja": "2つの視覚モデルを並べて提示することで、講師は通常なら見落とされかねない違いを強調できます。",
          "type": "inference",
          "points": 40
        },
        {
          "text": "A positive correlation between variables does not necessarily establish that one variable directly causes the other.",
          "grammar": "not necessarily / establish that",
          "ja": "変数間に正の相関があっても、一方が他方を直接引き起こすことが必ずしも証明されるわけではありません。",
          "type": "inference",
          "points": 40
        },
        {
          "text": "The straight and curved arrows may be intended to distinguish a direct relationship from one involving an additional mechanism.",
          "grammar": "may be intended to / distinguish A from B",
          "ja": "直線と曲線の矢印は、直接的な関係と追加的な仕組みを伴う関係を区別するためのものかもしれません。",
          "type": "inference",
          "points": 40
        },
        {
          "text": "Such a distinction is nuanced because the concepts are related and may initially appear almost interchangeable.",
          "grammar": "because / may appear＋形容詞",
          "ja": "これらの概念は関連しており、一見するとほとんど同じように見える可能性があるため、その区別は微妙です。",
          "type": "inference",
          "points": 40
        },
        {
          "text": "Rather than merely stating that the concepts differ, the lecturer is using visual evidence to delineate precisely how they differ.",
          "grammar": "Rather than＋動名詞 / how節",
          "ja": "講師は単に概念が異なると述べるのではなく、視覚的な資料を使って具体的にどのように異なるのかを明らかにしています。",
          "type": "gist",
          "points": 40
        },
        {
          "text": "Overall, the scene provides useful practice in elaborating on nuanced distinctions, differentiating related concepts, interpreting statistical relationships, and explaining subtle conceptual differences.",
          "grammar": "動名詞列挙",
          "ja": "全体として、この場面は微妙な違いを詳しく説明すること、関連概念を区別すること、統計的関係を解釈すること、細かな概念差を説明することの練習に適しています。",
